<description>
Sort the 5x5 marker fragments into the 3x3 slots indicated by their orientations and complete any missing symmetric fragments.

Input structure
The grid is a 19x19 canvas split by black separator rows and columns into a 3x3 array of 5x5 tiles.
Inside the tiles there are exactly two nonblack colors: a frequent fill color and a less frequent marker color.
Nonblank marker masks are fragments whose centroid direction relative to the 5x5 center names one of the nine slots.

Rule
Classify each nonblank marker mask by the signs of its row and column offsets from the tile center: top/center/bottom and left/center/right.
For every output slot, collect all dihedral symmetries of the known fragments that would land in that slot, assert they agree, and use that mask.
Rebuild the same separated 3x3 tile canvas with each completed mask in its classified slot.

Key insight
The input is a shuffled library of symmetric tile fragments; each fragment's centroid direction is its target position.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "nonblank marker mask s inside a 5x5 tile",
  "dst": "5x5 tile slot d in the ordered 3x3 tile array",
  "match_cond": "sign(s.marker_centroid - tile_center) == d.position relative to the array center",
  "transform": "move each mask to its matched slot; generate absent slots by the agreed dihedral symmetry of known masks in the same orbit; refill tile backgrounds with the frequent nonblack color"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: fixed 19x19; black (0) separator rows/cols at indices 0,6,12,18 form a 3x3 array of 5x5 tiles
  colors: exactly 2 non-black colors; fill_color (more frequent) and marker_color (less frequent); every tile cell is one of these two
  masks:
    description: |
      Three seed patterns define all 9 tile masks via dihedral (D4) symmetry:
      1. corner_seed: non-empty boolean pattern in the top-left 2x2 of a 5x5 tile, diagonal-symmetric (transpose-symmetric). 1-4 cells. Centroid direction is (-1,-1).
      2. edge_seed: non-empty boolean pattern in the top 2 rows of a 5x5 tile, left-right symmetric about col 2. 1-10 cells. Centroid direction is (-1,0).
      3. center: equals union of all 8 D4 transforms of corner_seed. Always has full D4 symmetry. Middle row and middle col are always empty.
    corner_cells: 1-4 [observed]
    edge_cells: 2-6 [observed]
    center_cells: 4-16 (determined by corner_seed)
  output_layout: each tile position (tr,tc) maps to slot (tr-1,tc-1); the mask at slot (sr,sc) is placed at tile (sr+1,sc+1)
  orbit_generation: |
    Corners {(-1,-1),(-1,1),(1,-1),(1,1)}: all D4 transforms of corner_seed
    Edges {(-1,0),(0,-1),(0,1),(1,0)}: all D4 transforms of edge_seed
    Center {(0,0)}: union of D4 transforms of corner_seed
  input_vs_output: |
    Input: all 9 slot masks present but placed at SHUFFLED tile positions (random permutation of 9 slots across 9 tiles)
    Output: each mask moved to its correct tile position matching its centroid direction
    The masks themselves are unchanged between input and output
  shuffle: random permutation; 0-3 tiles may coincidentally be at correct position [observed]

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first, then shuffle
  steps:
    1. Pick 2 distinct non-black colors; assign more-frequent as fill_color, less-frequent as marker_color
    2. Design corner_seed as a random non-empty diagonal-symmetric pattern in a 2x2 grid (3 free bits, exclude all-zero -> 7 choices)
    3. Design edge_seed as a random non-empty LR-symmetric pattern in a 5x2 region (rows 0-1, 3 free cols per row -> 6 free bits, exclude all-zero -> 63 choices). Ensure centroid row < center (guaranteed since rows 0-1 only)
    4. Derive center mask = union of all 8 D4 transforms of corner_seed on 5x5
    5. Generate all 4 corner masks by D4-transforming corner_seed; generate all 4 edge masks by D4-transforming edge_seed
    6. Build 19x19 output grid with black separators and each mask placed at its correct slot tile
    7. Create input by randomly permuting the 9 tile contents across the 9 tile positions
```
